{title: At the Cross}
{artist: Isaac Watts & Ralph Hudson}
{key: E}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 76}

Verse 1
A[E]las! and did my [A]Savior [E]bleed, and did my Sovereign [B]die?
Would [E]he devote that [A]sacred [E]head for [A]sinners [B]such as [E]I?

Chorus
At the cross, at the cross, where I [A]first saw the light,
and the [E]burden of my heart rolled a[B]way —
it was [E]there by faith [A]I received my [E]sight,
and [C#m]now I [B]am happy [E]all the day!
